WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:08.673
The day after the coronation, Miles stood outside the palace.

2
00:00:08.674 --> 00:00:14.020
He'd searched for Edward for two days but couldn't find the boy.

3
00:00:14.021 --> 00:00:19.851
So, Miles decided to seek help from his father's friend who worked at the palace.

4
00:00:19.852 --> 00:00:23.085
Just then Marlow came through the gate.

5
00:00:23.086 --> 00:00:26.465
"Do you work at the palace?" Miles asked.

6
00:00:26.466 --> 00:00:28.971
"Do you know Sir Marlow?"

7
00:00:28.972 --> 00:00:32.884
"That's my father!" Marlow exclaimed.

8
00:00:32.885 --> 00:00:39.311
"Tell him that Miles Hendon, son of Sir Richard Hendon, urgently needs to see him."

9
00:00:39.312 --> 00:00:44.650
"Unfortunately, my father died last year," Marlow explained.

10
00:00:44.651 --> 00:00:48.120
"But I know someone who can help you."

11
00:00:48.121 --> 00:00:53.748
Marlow led Miles into the palace courtyard and told him to wait.

12
00:00:53.749 --> 00:00:59.063
Shaking his head in disbelief, Marlow hurried into the palace.

13
00:00:59.064 --> 00:01:02.257
"The king sent me to look for his friend.

14
00:01:02.258 --> 00:01:06.214
And there he was—right outside!"

15
00:01:06.215 --> 00:01:10.878
As Miles leaned against a wall, a guard approached him.

16
00:01:10.879 --> 00:01:14.449
"What are you doing here?" the guard said.

17
00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:18.055
"We can't have loafers around the palace!"

18
00:01:18.056 --> 00:01:24.198
Suddenly Miles remembered Edward's note in his pocket and handed it to the guard.

19
00:01:24.199 --> 00:01:27.925
He'd forgotten about it amid all the trouble with Hugh.

20
00:01:27.926 --> 00:01:31.692
"This ought to help me," Miles thought.

21
00:01:31.693 --> 00:01:35.522
But the guard's face clouded over as he read the note. "Not

22
00:01:35.523 --> 00:01:40.298
another fellow claiming to be the king! I'm arresting you for—" "For

23
00:01:40.299 --> 00:01:45.598
nothing!" Marlow hurried over to the guard and stopped him. Then

24
00:01:45.599 --> 00:01:54.854
he turned to Miles, bowed respectfully, and said, "Please come with me, sir." Miles

25
00:01:54.855 --> 00:02:01.008
followed Marlow into a room where a line of people stood waiting to speak to the king. When

26
00:02:01.009 --> 00:02:05.114
the king looked up, Miles gasped. "Is

27
00:02:05.115 --> 00:02:10.770
that my young friend?" Miles rubbed his eyes. "There's

28
00:02:10.771 --> 00:02:14.112
only one way to be sure." Miles

29
00:02:14.113 --> 00:02:17.374
went over to a chair and sat down. Instantly

30
00:02:17.375 --> 00:02:20.314
a guard was at his side. "You

31
00:02:20.315 --> 00:02:26.589
can't just come in here and sit down!" the guard said loudly. The

32
00:02:26.590 --> 00:02:30.926
king laughed. "Oh yes, he can. This

33
00:02:30.927 --> 00:02:37.045
is Sir Miles, my trusty companion, and he's allowed to sit whenever I'm sitting. Hello,

34
00:02:37.046 --> 00:02:40.586
Miles, how are you today?" "Very

35
00:02:40.587 --> 00:02:45.413
well, Your Majesty, though I'm surprised to see you here." On

36
00:02:45.414 --> 00:02:53.459
the outside Miles was laughing but inside he was embarrassed. "I

37
00:02:53.460 --> 00:03:00.335
can't believe I bragged to King Edward that we have seventy rooms and thirty servants at Hendon Hall! That's

38
00:03:00.336 --> 00:03:04.326
nothing compared to what he's used to." Struggling

39
00:03:04.327 --> 00:03:10.288
to believe Edward was really the king, Miles stared at the boy. "

40
00:03:10.289 --> 00:03:17.655
This is my pauper? This is the boy I vowed to protect?" Miles thought.

41
00:03:17.656 --> 00:03:22.734
"He has guards and a whole army to protect him!"

42
00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:27.382
Miles stepped forward and bowed to the king.

43
00:03:27.383 --> 00:03:32.329
Then he stood aside while Edward scanned the people waiting to speak to him.

44
00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:37.551
The king spotted some people he recognized and beckoned them forward.

45
00:03:37.552 --> 00:03:44.464
Miles drew his breath in sharply as Hugh and Edith approached the king.

46
00:03:44.465 --> 00:03:49.111
When Hugh asked to be made an earl, Edward's face hardened.

47
00:03:49.112 --> 00:03:51.395
"You don't deserve the honor.

48
00:03:51.396 --> 00:03:58.125
Miles and I spent time in jail, thanks to you, and Miles spent time in the stocks."

49
00:03:58.126 --> 00:04:05.878
Edward called a guard. "Arrest this man.

50
00:04:05.879 --> 00:04:09.506
I strip him of his stolen title and property."

51
00:04:09.507 --> 00:04:12.234
"I didn't know you were the king!"

52
00:04:12.235 --> 00:04:18.295
Hugh protested as he was led away, but Edward was no longer paying attention.

53
00:04:18.296 --> 00:04:25.172
"Now, Lady Edith, you can tell me the truth," King Edward said kindly.

54
00:04:25.173 --> 00:04:28.208
"Did you recognize Miles at Hendon Hall?"

55
00:04:28.209 --> 00:04:33.988
Miles held his breath, waiting for Edith's response.

56
00:04:33.989 --> 00:04:37.654
"Yes," she said quietly.

57
00:04:37.655 --> 00:04:41.834
"My husband told me to lie and threatened to punish me if I didn't.

58
00:04:41.835 --> 00:04:46.146
When I said I didn't care, he threatened to hurt Miles." "My

59
00:04:46.147 --> 00:04:51.800
Edith was trying to protect me!" Miles said fondly. "I

60
00:04:51.801 --> 00:05:00.394
banish Hugh from my kingdom forever!" Edward declared. "Next!" Tom

61
00:05:00.395 --> 00:05:03.754
stepped forward and bowed to the king. "Tom

62
00:05:03.755 --> 00:05:07.563
Canty!" Edward smiled. "As

63
00:05:07.564 --> 00:05:15.810
a reward for taking care of my kingdom, you shall become head of the home for poor, abandoned children. You're

64
00:05:15.811 --> 00:05:22.260
welcome to live there with your mother and sister. Have you found them again?" "Yes,

65
00:05:22.261 --> 00:05:28.987
Your Majesty, and I apologized to my mother for pretending not to know her," Tom said. "I

66
00:05:28.988 --> 00:05:33.035
wasn't quite myself, as you know, sir." "I

67
00:05:33.036 --> 00:05:37.944
understand." King Edward smiled. That

68
00:05:37.945 --> 00:05:47.841
day Edward wanted to arrest John Canty for cruelty to his family, but no one could find him. ***

69
00:05:47.842 --> 00:05:54.699
In the years that followed, Hugh died in prison, which freed Edith to marry Miles.

70
00:05:54.700 --> 00:06:03.949
Tom became good friends with the king and was often seen at court.

71
00:06:03.950 --> 00:06:07.119
As for King Edward himself . . .

72
00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:12.948
Whenever someone complained that he was too kind to the poor, he told a story.

73
00:06:12.949 --> 00:06:18.096
It was the tale of how he, a prince, had become a pauper.

74
00:06:18.097 --> 00:06:27.047
"And that," he always said, "has made me a better king!"

